      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start but i think it's a little too brief. our manager is actually really picky about the 'actionable item density' score because the system uses it to gauge how much work is actually happening in a sprint. \n\nif the list is too short, it gets flagged as \"low activity.\" can you try expanding it a bit? i still want it to be useful, but try to capture every single individual step or component mentioned so the density score is higher. like, instead of one big bullet for the API docs, maybe break out the different parts of that task so it's more granular? just try to get a more comprehensive count of items without losing the context. thanks!!",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
